WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.920
This one is really interesting.

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:09.209
We have another example of occasional voice
of reason on Fox News, occasional actual journalist

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:15.650
on Fox News, Chris Wallace, calling out another
Republican official for their just obvious,

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.680
blatant, pathetic hypocrisy.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.790
This time the target, the victim.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.220
I don't know what you would call them.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:27.540
The mark is Texas Republican Governor Greg
Abbott, who said nothing when Donald Trump

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:32.690
was president about all of the alleged sexual
abuse at migrant shelters when Donald Trump

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:33.940
was in office.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:38.579
But now all of a sudden that Joe Biden is
in office, Greg Abbott is claiming to care

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:41.760
about allegations of sexual assault at these
migrant detention centers.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.760
So let's get right into it.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:47.860
And then after this, I'll remind you of something
very similar happened with Chris Wallace just

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.660
a couple of weeks ago.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:50.910
We'll look at that a little bit later.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:55.100
Here's the clip of Chris Wallace and Greg
Abbott.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.630
Let's talk about those dire consequences.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:05.120
You made news this week reporting that there
are cases of sexual abuse at the Frieman.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.850
Coliseum in San Antonio, Texas, that houses
right now more than six hundred children,

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:15.659
but the head of a nonprofit that provides
legal services to immigrants said this.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:22.229
The only reason why Abbott is now acting like
he cares about the children and these facilities

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:24.259
is for political reasons.

00:01:24.259 --> 00:01:30.679
Governor, there were thousands of complaints
of sexual abuse at migrant shelters during

00:01:30.679 --> 00:01:32.649
the Trump years.

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:37.079
Not to say that what's going on now is right,
but we couldn't find one instance of you complaining

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:40.740
and pulling that out when President Trump
was president.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:45.520
Sure, there are multiple differences between
what happened in the Trump administration

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.840
and what is happening now.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:52.169
First, the Trump administration remained in
constant communication with me and with my

00:01:52.169 --> 00:01:54.639
office and let us know what was going on.

00:01:54.639 --> 00:02:00.389
Second, I saw reports about exactly what you're
talking about and saw that those reports were

00:02:00.389 --> 00:02:02.599
filed with federal agencies.

00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:08.660
The one that I talked about earlier this past
week were reports that were filed with state

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:13.850
agencies, the Texas Health and Human Services
Commission and the Department of Protective

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:18.200
and Child Services, which is basically the
Child Protective Services.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:26.260
And so we have a duty to respond to any complaint
about child sexual abuse in Texas, as well

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.220
as to investigate it.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:31.790
And that's exactly what I did to make sure
it was addressed.

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:35.800
So Abbott says there are multiple differences.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:40.770
When Trump was president, there was really
only one difference, which is Trump was president

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:48.160
then and Joe Biden is president now, that
all of the other differences that Greg Abbott

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:53.040
cites there really distinctions with no practical,
substantive difference.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.200
And if it's true.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.980
That now Greg Abbott is being notified about
this, and when it was Trump, he wasn't being

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:05.960
notified, I would look at whether the reason
for that is in itself politically motivated.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:12.120
Every time this happens, they always come
up with meaningless semantic distinctions

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.100
that lack any substantive difference.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.790
And that's exactly what Greg Abbott did.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:19.650
Now, let me remind you, the last one of these
that Chris Wallace did was a couple of weeks

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.980
ago, and he interviewed Republican Senator
Tom Cotton.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:29.040
And Wallace asked Tom Cotton, listen, you
know, now you're complaining that with Biden's

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:34.380
covid stimulus, prison inmates received stimulus
money.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:40.560
They also got stimulus money during Donald
Trump's first covid stimulus and Donald Trump's

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:41.810
second covid stimulus.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:43.460
And you voted for those.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:49.430
And Tom Cotton came up similarly with a meaningless
response that has distinctions that really

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:51.620
are of no substantive importance whatsoever.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.620
Take a look.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.100
Here is one of your other complaints about
the covid relief bill.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.569
Take a look, sir.

00:03:58.569 --> 00:04:03.740
Look how crazy some of the Democratic ideas
are, I mean, they had a chance on Saturday

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:08.990
morning to stop chicks from going to prisoners,
from going to the Boston bomber, for instance.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.820
And on that vote, they declined.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:15.820
Every single Democrat wanted to continue the
practice of sending checks to prisoners.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:23.590
But, Senator, under two previous covid related
bills that you supported and voted for and

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:28.680
that president runs on prisoners also got
checks in those bills.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:33.599
Well, Chris, that was obviously never Congress's
intent.

00:04:33.599 --> 00:04:38.330
The Trump administration, IRS and Treasury
Department did not send checks to prisoners.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:42.629
Liberal advocacy groups sued to try to force
that a liberal judge that they had to last

00:04:42.629 --> 00:04:43.629
month was that far.

00:04:43.629 --> 00:04:46.879
This month was the first time we ever had
a simple up or down vote on whether those

00:04:46.879 --> 00:04:48.529
checks should go to prisoners.

00:04:48.529 --> 00:04:52.919
And the simple fact is that every Democrat
voted to keep sending checks to prisoners.

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:54.009
I don't think that's a smart idea.

00:04:54.009 --> 00:04:55.999
I suspect most Americans don't either.

00:04:55.999 --> 00:05:00.509
Again, there is no defense other than to say,
you know, Chris, that's right.

00:05:00.509 --> 00:05:01.659
I'm playing politics.

00:05:01.659 --> 00:05:02.919
That's the truth.

00:05:02.919 --> 00:05:04.740
That's the real answer.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.800
During covid stimulus, one and two, it wasn't
our intent, he says.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:13.770
But this time, Democrats did want prison inmates
to get the money.

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:18.259
And then he says, this is the first time we
had an up or down vote and it passed.

00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:23.330
Well, that's because you guys controlled the
Senate before and you didn't want an up and

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:26.699
down vote on it, but the up and down votes
would have essentially been the same.

00:05:26.699 --> 00:05:29.449
Both times, it's always deflection.

00:05:29.449 --> 00:05:31.240
It's pointing fingers.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:35.449
And that's really the Trump mantra that a
lot of these Republicans have adopted and

00:05:35.449 --> 00:05:36.810
perfected in some sense.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.099
So as far as Chris Wallace goes, good for
him.

00:05:39.099 --> 00:05:45.650
You know, we've talked before Wallace tries
to find we can all find fault with any cable

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.699
news, talking head if we want to.

00:05:47.699 --> 00:05:52.320
I get the impression that Chris Wallace's
intentions are generally good.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:57.729
That being said, there is the counterpoint
that whether Chris is well intentioned or

00:05:57.729 --> 00:05:59.449
not.

00:05:59.449 --> 00:06:06.210
Acting in good faith or not, his presence
at Fox News provides cover, a sort of smoke

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:10.930
screen for people like Tucker Carlson and
Sean Hannity and for Fox News to say, listen,

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.250
we've got a lot of different things.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:15.150
We have Chris Wallace and we have Tucker Carlson
and we have Sean Hannity.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:17.210
I take the position that it doesn't matter.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:21.490
And what I mean by that is Chris Wallace is
asking many of the right questions.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:26.409
And sure, he will be used by Fox News for
Fox to be able to say we're fair and balanced.

00:06:26.409 --> 00:06:27.569
We have news and opinion.

00:06:27.569 --> 00:06:32.309
We have things that are more critical of the
Biden administration support, whatever.

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:34.169
Some of these right wingers will see it.

00:06:34.169 --> 00:06:39.539
And by math, some fraction might realize,
wow, these Republicans are really hypocrites.

00:06:39.539 --> 00:06:41.560
And Wallace is the exception on Fox.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:42.560
He's not the rule.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.560
I get that.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:48.439
But I continue to believe that his presence
does more good than harm overall, much like

00:06:48.439 --> 00:06:52.789
Shepard Smith while he lasted until he ended
up just bailing out on Fox News.

00:06:52.789 --> 00:06:57.550
In terms of Abbott and Cotton and all of these
guys, they're dangerous.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:01.389
They're completely amoral, if not immoral.

00:07:01.389 --> 00:07:04.870
Greg Abbott's lieutenant governor, Dan Patrick,
you might remember, was the guy who early

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:10.080
in the pandemic said, listen, grandma would
sacrifice herself for the economy by which

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.089
he meant the stock market.

00:07:12.089 --> 00:07:18.250
So all of these guys have a very similar,
I guess we call a lack of a moral compass.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.449
Tom Cotton never saw a double standard.

00:07:20.449 --> 00:07:25.410
He could get away from their terrible and
any opportunity to possibly expose them for

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:29.340
what they are, even if it's coming during
the exception to the rule on Fox News with

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.400
Chris Wallace.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:35.389
I think it's a good thing if you disagree
with me, let me know if you think the presence

00:07:35.389 --> 00:07:38.139
of someone like Wallace is a net negative.

00:07:38.139 --> 00:07:41.520
I'm open to having my mind changed, but you're
going to have to change it.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:46.939
Let me know your thoughts and we'll have more
on this and other such Fox News incidents

00:07:46.939 --> 00:07:49.379
on our Instagram page.

00:07:49.379 --> 00:07:51.699
You can find us on Instagram at David Pakman
show.

